        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PscsConnectionKind.Nfc">
            <summary>
                The smart card is connected through a Near-Field Communication (NFC) reader.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnectionFactory">
            <summary>Creates raw smart-card connections for an enumerated PC/SC device.</summary>
            <remarks>
                If <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnectionFactory.CreateAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice,System.Threading.CancellationToken)" /> fails or is cancelled before returning a connection, the factory must clean up
                every partial native resource it acquired. If it cannot prove that cleanup completed, it must throw
                <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.UnrecoveredConnectionException" />; Core then retains the managed physical-device claim.
                Ordinary creation failures mean the factory proved its own partial resources released and permit retry.
                This creation-failure signal does not apply to disposal: any smart-card disposal failure remains unproven.
            </remarks>
            <remarks>
                A returned connection must not complete disposal until it has relinquished every native resource it owns.
                If disposal throws, Core cannot infer release from the exception type and retains any managed physical-device
                claim associated with that connection.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnectionFactory.CreateAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Creates and initializes a smart-card connection.</summary>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.UnrecoveredConnectionException">
                Creation failed after acquiring native resources whose release the factory could not prove.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IRegisteredSmartCardConnectionFactory">
            <summary>Creates a smart-card connection while owning its physical registration.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Implementations accept ownership of the registration on every exit, including failure and cancellation:
                release it only after native release is proven; otherwise retain it and mark it unrecovered.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory">
            <summary>The built-in smart-card connection factory.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Custom factories implement <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnectionFactory" /> rather than deriving from this type.
                Configure connection logging through <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.YubiKitLogging" />.
                Without an explicit sharing policy, new factories snapshot <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing" />, initially
                <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Exclusive" />. Contention fails with <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionInUseException" />
                rather than retrying shared access. All built-in sharing modes request card power-off on release.
                Direct <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.CreateAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice,System.Threading.CancellationToken)" /> calls do not acquire the physical-device ownership guard used by
                <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Abstractions.IYubiKey.ConnectAsync``1(System.Threading.CancellationToken)" />. Coordinate discovery, including background
                monitoring, and other connections to the key for the full direct connection lifetime. With shared
                access, a discovery metadata read or another handle can select a different applet and disturb a session.
                Prefer <c>device.ConnectAsync&lt;ISmartCardConnection&gt;()</c> for SDK-managed ownership; the sharing policy
                still determines whether other processes can open the card.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing">
            <summary>
                The <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing" /> used by factories created without an explicit mode, including the
                one behind <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.YubiKeyManager" />. Defaults to <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Exclusive" />.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                Set it once at start-up, before constructing factories or using <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.YubiKeyManager" />
                for discovery or monitoring. Existing factories and connections retain their selected policy.
                Migration: applications that require the former fallback behavior must explicitly select
                <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.ExclusiveWithSharedFallback" /> and accept shared card-wide security state.
                <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Shared" /> is also an explicit coexistence opt-in, not an isolation policy.
            </remarks>
            <example>
            <code>
            // Explicit compatibility opt-in, before any discovery or monitoring:
            SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing = SmartCardSharing.ExclusiveWithSharedFallback;
            var devices = await YubiKeyManager.FindAllAsync();
            </code>
            </example>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.#ctor">
            <summary>
                Creates a factory that uses the configured <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.YubiKitLogging" /> logger factory and
                <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing" />.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing)">
            <summary>Creates a factory that opens card handles with <paramref name="sharing"/>.</summary>
            <example>
            <code>
            // Explicitly accept shared access for this factory only:
            // Coordinate discovery/monitoring and all other connections to this key before opening directly.
            var factory = new SmartCardConnectionFactory(SmartCardSharing.Shared);
            await using var connection = await factory.CreateAsync(reader, cancellationToken);
            </code>
            </example>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing">
            <summary>
            How the SDK opens a PC/SC card handle (SCardConnect share mode).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Smart-card application state is card-wide, not per handle: NIST SP 800-73-5 Part 2 §2.4.2 lists the
            PIV PIN among the application security status indicators, so once a PIN is verified any handle on
            the card can use a PIN=ONCE key until the card is reset. By default the built-in SDK factory requires
            exclusive PC/SC access and fails with <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionInUseException" /> on contention,
            without a shared retry. PC/SC exclusivity excludes other PC/SC clients through the resource manager;
            it is not a guarantee about other transports or arbitrary custom connection implementations.
            All built-in modes request power-off on release (<c>SCARD_UNPOWER_CARD</c>) to clear card-wide state.
            Shared access permits other clients to use that state while the card remains powered;
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnection.IsExclusive" /> reports the acquired mode, and an explicitly selected
            fallback to shared access is logged as a warning.
            </para>
            <para>
            Set the process-wide mode through <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing" />, or pass one
            to <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing)" />. Applications migrating from the former
            fallback default must opt in explicitly if they need coexistence with other smart-card clients.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.ExclusiveWithSharedFallback">
            <summary>Explicit opt-in: open exclusively; on a sharing violation, retry shared and accept shared card-wide state.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Exclusive">
            <summary>The factory default: open exclusively or fail with <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionInUseException" />; never retry shared.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Shared">
            <summary>
            Open shared, for applications that must coexist with other smart-card users (gpg-agent, browsers,
            the OS smart-card service) and accept that card-wide state is reachable from their handles.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.UsbSmartCardConnection.IsExclusive">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Base32">
            <summary>Decodes RFC 4648 Base32 text without creating transformed text copies.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Accepts ASCII upper/lower case, ignores literal ASCII spaces, and accepts either complete padding
                or no padding. Unused bits in the last symbol are ignored, not required to be zero. Empty text is valid.
                Other whitespace, impossible terminal symbol counts, and incomplete or embedded padding are rejected.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Base32.Decode(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Char})">
            <summary>Decodes Base32 text into independently owned storage.</summary>
            <param name="encoded">The borrowed encoded text.</param>
            <returns>The decoded bytes. The caller must clear them when they contain secret material.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The text has invalid characters, length, or padding.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.OverflowException">The encoded text's byte length exceeds <see cref="F:System.Int32.MaxValue" />.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Base32.Decode(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Char},System.Span{System.Byte})">
            <summary>Decodes Base32 text into caller-owned storage and returns the number of bytes written.</summary>
            <param name="encoded">The borrowed encoded text.</param>
            <param name="destination">The output buffer, which must not overlap the encoded text's bytes; unused bytes are unchanged on success.</param>
            <returns>The number of decoded bytes written.</returns>
            <remarks>
                Admission rejects overlapping storage or an encoded byte length exceeding <see cref="F:System.Int32.MaxValue" />
                before decoding, leaving both spans unchanged. Once admitted, any decoding failure clears the entire
                destination, including any partially decoded prefix and unused tail. The borrowed text is never modified.
                On success, the caller owns the output and must clear secret material after use.
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The spans overlap, the text is malformed, or the destination is too small.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.OverflowException">The encoded text's byte length exceeds <see cref="F:System.Int32.MaxValue" />.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.BerLength">
            <summary>
            Utility for BER-TLV length encoding and decoding.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.BerLength.EncodingSize(System.Int32)">
            <summary>
            Returns the number of bytes needed to encode the given length (1, 2, or 3).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.BerLength.Write(System.Span{System.Byte},System.Int32)">
            <summary>
            Writes BER-TLV length into the destination span. Returns the number of bytes written.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Crc13239">
            <summary>
                Utility class for calculating and verifying the CRC13239 checksum used in YubiKey products.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Crc13239.Calculate(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
                Calculates a CRC13239 checksum over a byte buffer.
            </summary>
            <param name="buffer">The buffer to be checksummed.</param>
            <returns>A two byte CRC checksum.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableArrayPoolBuffer">
            <summary>
            A disposable buffer backed by <see cref="T:System.Buffers.ArrayPool`1"/> that securely clears memory on disposal.
            Implements <see cref="T:System.Buffers.IMemoryOwner`1"/> for compatibility with async APIs.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableArrayPoolBuffer.#ctor(System.Int32,System.Boolean)">
            <summary>
            Creates a new buffer of the specified size from the shared array pool.
            </summary>
            <param name="size">The size of the buffer to allocate.</param>
            <param name="clearOnCreate">If true, zeros the buffer after allocation. Defaults to true.</param>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentOutOfRangeException">Thrown when size is zero or negative.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableArrayPoolBuffer.Memory">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableArrayPoolBuffer.Span">
            <summary>
            Gets a span over the buffer's memory.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableArrayPoolBuffer.Length">
            <summary>
            Gets the logical length of the buffer.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableArrayPoolBuffer.CreateFromSpan(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Creates a buffer from a source span, copying the data.
            </summary>
            <param name="source">The source data to copy into the new buffer.</param>
            <returns>A new buffer containing a copy of the source data.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableArrayPoolBuffer.Dispose">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableBufferHandle">
            <summary>
                Wraps a <see cref="T:System.Memory`1"/> buffer and zeroes it when disposed.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                <b>Ownership transfer:</b> This type takes ownership of the provided buffer.
                The buffer is zeroed via <see cref="M:System.Security.Cryptography.CryptographicOperations.ZeroMemory(System.Span{System.Byte})"/>
                when <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableBufferHandle.Dispose"/> is called. Callers must not read from or write to
                the original <paramref name="data"/> after disposing this handle.
                Always pass a freshly-allocated or rented buffer — never wrap caller-held memory
                that must survive beyond the scope of this handle.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableBufferHandle.#ctor(System.Memory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
                Wraps a <see cref="T:System.Memory`1"/> buffer and zeroes it when disposed.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                <b>Ownership transfer:</b> This type takes ownership of the provided buffer.
                The buffer is zeroed via <see cref="M:System.Security.Cryptography.CryptographicOperations.ZeroMemory(System.Span{System.Byte})"/>
                when <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableBufferHandle.Dispose"/> is called. Callers must not read from or write to
                the original <paramref name="data"/> after disposing this handle.
                Always pass a freshly-allocated or rented buffer — never wrap caller-held memory
                that must survive beyond the scope of this handle.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableTlvList">
            <summary>
                A disposable collection of TLV objects that ensures all contained TLVs are properly disposed.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                This class is used to manage the lifetime of multiple TLV objects, ensuring that sensitive
                cryptographic data is properly zeroed out when no longer needed.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableTlvList.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv[])">
            <summary>
                Creates a new collection with the specified TLV objects.
            </summary>
            <param name="tlvs">The TLV objects to include in the collection.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableTlvList.#ctor(System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable{Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv})">
            <summary>
                Creates a new collection from an enumerable of TLV objects.
            </summary>
            <param name="tlvs">The TLV objects to include in the collection.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableTlvList.Dispose">
            <summary>
                Disposes all TLV objects in the collection, securely zeroing their data.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableTlvList.Item(System.Int32)">
            <summary>
                Gets the TLV object at the specified index.
            </summary>
            <param name="index">The zero-based index of the TLV to get.</param>
            <returns>The TLV at the specified index.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableTlvList.Count">
            <summary>
                Gets the number of TLV objects in the collection.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableTlvList.GetEnumerator">
            <summary>
                Returns an enumerator that iterates through the collection.
            </summary>
            <returns>An enumerator for the collection.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.DisposableTlvList.AsSpan">
            <summary>
                Returns a span view of the collection for efficient iteration.
            </summary>
            <returns>A span containing all TLV objects in the collection.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.ExchangeGuard">
            <summary>
                Refuses overlapping logical exchanges against a stateful sequential peer (a smart card or HID device).
                Callers wrap a <em>complete</em> multi-step exchange so no foreign traffic can interleave it on the
                shared underlying connection.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                <para>
                    Sessions support one operation at a time. An overlapping caller receives an
                    <see cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException" /> immediately rather than waiting. Once entered, the exchange
                    runs to completion: the delegate receives
                    <see cref="P:System.Threading.CancellationToken.None" />, so a caller's token can never abort a logical exchange
                    between its constituent transmits (which would strand chained command/response or SCP MAC state
                    on the card and poison the next caller's exchange).
                </para>
                <para>
                    The guard must not be re-entered from within a running exchange. Keep the wrapped delegate confined
                    to transport/processor calls that never call back into guarded methods.
                </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.ExchangeGuard.RunAsync``1(System.Func{System.Threading.CancellationToken,System.Threading.Tasks.Task{``0}},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
                Runs <paramref name="exchange" /> exclusively; overlapping calls are refused immediately.
                A pre-canceled <paramref name="cancellationToken" /> throws before the guard is claimed.
                The delegate is invoked with <see cref="P:System.Threading.CancellationToken.None" /> so the in-flight exchange always
                completes.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.ExchangeGuard.RunAsync(System.Func{System.Threading.CancellationToken,System.Threading.Tasks.Task},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
                Result-free overload of <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.ExchangeGuard.RunAsync``1(System.Func{System.Threading.CancellationToken,System.Threading.Tasks.Task{``0}},System.Threading.CancellationToken)" /> for exchanges whose only purpose is their side
                effect (lazy initialization, for example).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.ExchangeGuard.Run(System.Action)">
            <summary>Runs a synchronous state mutation under the same close-aware admission as an exchange.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.ExchangeGuard.CloseAndDrain">
            <summary>Refuses future admissions and synchronously waits for an admitted exchange to finish.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.ExchangeGuard.CloseAndDrainAsync">
            <summary>Refuses future admissions and asynchronously waits for an admitted exchange to finish.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.MultiString">
            <summary>
                Utilities for working with multi null-terminated strings.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.MultiString.GetStrings(System.Byte[],System.Text.Encoding)">
            <summary>
                Converts the byte array representing a multi-null-terminated string and return them as
                .NET strings.
            </summary>
            <param name="value">Multi-string to convert.</param>
            <param name="encoding">Encoding to use for interpreting the strings.</param>
            <returns>Array of converted strings.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.MultiString.GetBytes(System.String[],System.Text.Encoding)">
            <summary>
                Converts an array of strings to a multi-null-terminated string.
            </summary>
            <param name="value">Array of strings.</param>
            <param name="encoding">Encoding to apply to the multi-string.</param>
            <returns>Byte array containing multi-string.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv">
            <summary>
                Tag, length, Value structure that helps to parse APDU response data.
                This class handles BER-TLV encoded data with determinate length.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.#ctor(System.Int32,System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
                Creates a new TLV (Tag-Length-Value) object with the specified tag and value.
            </summary>
            <param name="tag">The tag value, must be between 0x00 and 0xFFFF.</param>
            <param name="value">The value data as a read-only span of bytes.</param>
            <remarks>
                This constructor creates a BER-TLV encoded structure where:
                - The tag is encoded in the minimum number of bytes needed
                - The length is encoded according to BER-TLV rules
                - The value is stored as provided
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.Tag">
            <summary>
                Returns the tag.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.Value">
            <summary>
                Returns a copy of the value.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.Length">
            <summary>
                Returns the length of the value.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.TotalLength">
            <summary>
                Returns the total length of the TLV object.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.Dispose">
            <summary>
                Dispose the object and clears its buffers
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.AsMemory">
            <summary>
                Retrieves the internal byte array of the TLV object as a Memory&lt;byte&gt;>.
            </summary>
            <returns>
                A Memory&lt;byte&gt; instance representing the underlying data of the TLV object.
            </returns>
            <remarks>
                This method provides a view of the TLV's internal data, allowing for efficient
                access and manipulation of the bytes without copying the data.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.AsSpan">
            <summary>
                Returns a read-only span representing the internal byte array of the TLV object.
            </summary>
            <returns>
                A <see cref="T:System.ReadOnlySpan`1" /> containing the full encoded TLV data, including the tag,
                length, and value.
            </returns>
            <remarks>
                The returned span includes all components of the TLV structure, and its size equals the total
                length of the encoded TLV.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.Create(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
                Parse a Tlv from a BER-TLV encoded byte array.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">A byte array containing the TLV encoded data (and nothing more).</param>
            <returns>The parsed Tlv</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv.ToString">
            <summary>
                Returns a string that represents the current object.
            </summary>
            <returns>A string that represents the current object.</returns>
            <remarks>
                The string is of the form <c>Tlv(0xTAG, LENGTH, VALUE)</c>.
                <para>
                    The tag is written out in hexadecimal, prefixed by 0x.
                    The length is written out in decimal.
                    The value is written out in hexadecimal.
                </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.TlvHelper">
            <summary>
                Utility methods to encode and decode BER-TLV data.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.TlvHelper.DecodeList(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
                Decodes a sequence of BER-TLV encoded data into a disposable collection of Tlvs.
            </summary>
            <param name="tlvData">Sequence of TLV encoded data</param>
            <returns>A disposable collection of <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv" /> objects that must be disposed to securely clear sensitive data.</returns>
            <remarks>
                The returned collection must be disposed using a <c>using</c> declaration to ensure
                all TLV objects are properly disposed and their sensitive data is securely zeroed.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.TlvHelper.DecodeDictionary(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
                Decodes a sequence of BER-TLV encoded data into a mapping of Tag-Value pairs.
                Iteration order is preserved. If the same tag occurs more than once only the latest will be kept.
            </summary>
            <param name="tlvData">Sequence of TLV encoded data</param>
            <returns>Dictionary of Tag-Value pairs</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.TlvHelper.EncodeList(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv[])">
            <summary>
                Encodes a list of Tlvs into a sequence of BER-TLV encoded data.
            </summary>
            <param name="tlvData">List of Tlvs to encode</param>
            <returns>
                A caller-owned buffer containing the BER-TLV encoded list, or an empty buffer if
                <paramref name="tlvData" /> contains no elements. The caller must securely clear the returned
                buffer when it contains sensitive data.
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentNullException">
                <paramref name="tlvData" /> is <see langword="null" />, or contains a <see langword="null" /> element.
            </exception>
            <remarks>
                This method does not dispose the input <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv" /> objects. The caller remains responsible
                for disposing them. Source buffers used to construct the TLVs also remain caller-owned and are not
                cleared by this method.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.TlvHelper.EncodeAndDisposeList(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv[])">
            <summary>
                Encodes a collection of TLV objects into a single byte sequence, then disposes each TLV.
                Use this when the TLV objects are created inline and not needed after encoding.
            </summary>
            <param name="tlvData">TLVs to encode and dispose. Each TLV is disposed even if encoding fails.</param>
            <returns>
                A caller-owned buffer containing the BER-TLV encoded list, or an empty buffer if
                <paramref name="tlvData" /> contains no elements. The caller must securely clear the returned
                buffer when it contains sensitive data.
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentNullException">
                <paramref name="tlvData" /> is <see langword="null" />, or contains a <see langword="null" /> element.
            </exception>
            <remarks>
                Source buffers used to construct the TLVs remain caller-owned and are not cleared by this method.
                Disposing the input TLVs does not clear the returned buffer.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.TlvHelper.GetValue(System.Int32,System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
                Decode a single TLV encoded object, returning only the value.
            </summary>
            <param name="expectedTag">The expected tag value of the given TLV data</param>
            <param name="tlvData">The TLV data</param>
            <returns>
                A caller-owned buffer containing the TLV value. The caller must securely clear the returned
                buffer when it contains sensitive data.
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException">If the TLV tag differs from expectedTag</exception>
            <remarks>
                The returned buffer is a copy and remains valid after the internal <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Tlv" /> is disposed.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.TlvHelper.TryFindValue(System.Int32,System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.Memory{System.Byte}@)">
            <summary>
                Searches a sequence of TLV encoded data for a specific tag and returns its value.
            </summary>
            <param name="tag">The tag to search for</param>
            <param name="tlvData">Sequence of TLV encoded data</param>
            <param name="value">The value of the first TLV with the matching tag, or default if not found</param>
            <returns>True if the tag was found, false otherwise</returns>
            <remarks>
                When this method returns <see langword="true" />, <paramref name="value" /> is a caller-owned buffer.
                The caller must securely clear it when it contains sensitive data.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.TlvHelper.EncodeDictionary(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Byte[]})">
            <summary>
                Encodes a mapping of tag-value pairs into BER-TLV data ordered by ascending tag.
            </summary>
            <param name="tlvData">Dictionary of TLV tag-value pairs.</param>
            <returns>
                A caller-owned buffer containing the BER-TLV encoded dictionary, or an empty buffer if
                <paramref name="tlvData" /> contains no elements. The caller must securely clear the returned
                buffer when it contains sensitive data.
            </returns>
            <remarks>
                Source buffers used as dictionary values remain caller-owned and are not cleared by this method.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.YubiKitLogging.Configure(Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILoggerFactory)">
            <summary>
            Configures YubiKit logging with the provided logger factory.
            Call this method once at application startup before using SDK services.
            </summary>
            <param name="loggerFactory">The logger factory to use, or null for no logging.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.YubiKitLogging.UseTemporary(Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILoggerFactory)">
            <summary>
            Temporarily replaces the LoggerFactory. Dispose to restore. Useful for testing.
            </summary>
        </member>
    </members>
</doc>
